# Aorist Stems — Memory Drill

## Purpose

Drill present→aorist stem mapping for suppletive and irregular verbs. These forms cannot be derived from the present stem — they must be memorised cold.

Prompt format: present tense (English gloss) → aorist sg1
Example: "eat (τρώω) → ?" → "έφαγα"

## Why this belongs in memory drills

Regular aorist (-σα pattern: δουλεύω→δούλεψα) can be computed from the present stem and does not belong here. Suppletive and irregular stems are arbitrary mappings. The learning sequence explicitly flags these as "must be memorised."

## Phase 2 core set (Phase 2 prerequisite)

Implemented as 15 items in `aorist-stems.tsx`, forward prompt `label` = "English (present)".

| Present | Aorist sg1 | Category (`category`) |
|---------|------------|-----------|
| τρώω    | έφαγα      | suppletive |
| πίνω    | ήπια       | suppletive |
| βλέπω   | είδα       | suppletive |
| πηγαίνω / πάω | πήγα | suppletive |
| λέω     | είπα       | suppletive |
| έρχομαι | ήρθα       | irregular |
| κάνω    | έκανα      | irregular |
| παίρνω  | πήρα       | irregular |
| φεύγω   | έφυγα      | irregular |
| βρίσκω  | βρήκα      | irregular |
| δίνω    | έδωσα      | irregular |
| μαθαίνω | έμαθα      | irregular |
| μένω    | έμεινα     | irregular |
| καταλαβαίνω | κατάλαβα | irregular |
| στέλνω  | έστειλα    | irregular |

Predictable -σα / -ψα aorists (γράφω → έγραψα, διαβάζω → διάβασα) are not in this drill; they
belong to Aorist formation (`aorist-formation.tsx`).

## Drill modes

**Forward**: Given English meaning + present form → produce aorist sg1
  - "eat (τρώω) → ?"  → "έφαγα"

**Reverse**: Given aorist sg1 → recall present / English meaning, self-assess
  - "ήπια → ?"  → "drink (πίνω)"

## Grouping

Filter categories on the config screen: Suppletive (5, hardest, highest priority), Irregular (10),
or All.

## Time limits

No per-drill limit. Timing is the learner's Fast 4 s / Medium 6 s / Relaxed 8 s choice on the config
screen, plus 35% for each extra word in a forward answer (`src/routes/practice/components/drill-speeds.ts`).
Every answer here is one word, so the surcharge never applies.

## Notes

- Drill as complete aorist sg1 forms, not "stems" — the augment is part of what must be recalled
- Do not mix regular -σα verbs into this drill
- Future forms (θα φάω, θα πιω) share the same stem — once aorist is learned, future comes almost free. A post-session note saying so is not implemented
